
P6
=======

🔹 Problem Statement: Group, Country, and Business Category-Based Access Restriction in PingFederate
In a PingFederate SSO integration, access to specific applications must be controlled using a combination of user group membership, country, and business category attributes. The system should apply conditional logic to determine whether a user is allowed to access the application.

🔸 Requirements:
The user must be a member of a specific LDAP group, such as:

CN=ABC,OU=Groups,DC=abc,DC=com

If the group matches, the user's access should then be evaluated based on:

Country: Only allow users from approved countries like DE, CN, BE, BR, BG, etc.

Business Category:

If the user’s country is DE, only allow access if their businessCategory is not Marketing.

For all other approved countries, allow access without business category check.

If none of the conditions match or the user does not belong to the specified group, access should be denied by default.

The OGNL expression must be used in Issuance Criteria and trigger an Error Result like "AccessDenied" when conditions are not met.



Solution:


#access = @java.lang.Boolean@FALSE,  // Initialize access flag as FALSE

#groups = #this.get("ds.ldap.memberOf") != null ? #this.get("ds.ldap.memberOf").getValues() : {},

#groups.{
    #group = #this,
    #group = new javax.naming.ldap.LdapName(#group),

    // Check for specific group membership (case-insensitive match)
    #group.toString().matches("(?i).*CN=ABC,OU=Groups,DC=abc,DC=com.*") ?

    (
        // Country must not be null
        #this.get("country") != null ?

        (
            // Check if user is from an approved country
            #this.get("country").toString().matches("(?i)CN|DE|BE|BR|BG|CA|CY|CZ|DK|EE") ?

            (
                // Special handling for Germany (DE)
                #this.get("country").toString().equalsIgnoreCase("DE") ?

                (
                    // If from DE, allow access only if businessCategory is NOT "Consumer Healthcare"
                    #this.get("ds.ldap.businessCategory") != null &&
                    !#this.get("ds.ldap.businessCategory").hasValue("Marketing") ?
                    (#access = @java.lang.Boolean@TRUE) :
                    (#access = @java.lang.Boolean@FALSE)
                )

                :

                // For all other countries, allow access
                (#access = @java.lang.Boolean@TRUE)
            )

            :

            // If country is not in the approved list
            (#access = @java.lang.Boolean@FALSE)
        )

        :

        // If country is null
        (#access = @java.lang.Boolean@FALSE)
    )

    :

    // If group does not match
    {}
},

#access  // Return final access decision (true or false)
